                <pb facs="0513" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/699: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Chihuahua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Myers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-14T19:00:00-06:00">April 14, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 16—4:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>General Almazan troop and passenger trains left last night for Ciudad Juarez. The
                    state treasurer published notices today in local papers declaring void all taxes
                    paid from March 3rd to date and demanding that such be paid again
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
